<p class="para lt-chem-349756" id="av_1.0-ch16_s04_s02_p67">Lactic acid (CH<sub>3</sub>CH(OH)CO<sub>2</sub>H) is a weak acid with a p<em>K</em><sub>a</sub> of 3.86 at 25&deg;C. What percentage of the lactic acid is ionized in each solution?</p>

